CORE SUBMODULE (Not Third-Party)
================================
Name:       Aether-RAG (Lightweight Embedding-Augmented Neural Neighbor)
Version:    Internal
Author:     Krish Dokania
License:    MIT (see LICENSE in this directory)

Purpose:
  Provides hybrid semantic search (dense embeddings + BM25 sparse
  retrieval + learned fusion) for AetherArena's file indexing, memory
  retrieval, and RAG pipeline. 
  
  Note: Unlike other services in the `services/` directory which are true 
  third-party vendored dependencies, Aether-RAG is an original core 
  component of the AetherArena stack, authored by Krish Dokania. It is 
  structured as an independent package to maintain isolation and allow 
  it to be released under the permissive MIT license, separate from the 
  rest of the AetherArena repository.

Modification policy:
  - Aether-RAG packages live under packages/ with their own test suites.
  - AetherArena integrates via core/integrations/providers/aether_rag/.
  - TODO/FIXME comments in Aether-RAG packages are Aether-RAG roadmap items.
  - Keep all code in this directory compliant with the MIT license.
